diff --git b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
index df48c0e..655ce59 100644
--- b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
+++ a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@ The table above is the short list. This part covers the remaining `MOE_CACHE_*`
 | `MOE_CACHE_PROFILE_DECAY` | A number from 0 to 1: how much of the previously learned expert-usage profile is kept when it is combined with this session's usage when the profile is saved (0 forgets old usage, 1 keeps it fully). Bad values are ignored with a warning. | 0.5 | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_PROMPT_CACHE_MIB` | Sets llama-server's prompt cache size (`--cache-ram`) in MiB, replacing the launcher's rule. Only a plain whole number counts; 0 turns the prompt cache off. | Unset (0 under 16 GB of server RAM, otherwise 2048 MiB) | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_PROXY_KEEPALIVE` | Only when exactly `1`: the on-demand proxy keeps one connection per client thread and server port and reuses it for the next request, instead of opening a new one each time. | Off | advanced |
+| `MOE_CACHE_REFILL_AFTER_PROMPT` | A number above 0 makes the cache refill start sooner after a long prompt (after an eighth of the usual idle wait, at least 20 ms), so the generation working set is ready earlier. | Off | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_SLOT_SIMILARITY` | Launcher: a new request may take over a busy conversation's slot only if its prompt is at least this similar (0 to 1) to what the slot holds, so a short request from another agent does not push out a long conversation. Passed on as `--slot-prompt-similarity`. | unset (llama-server's own default). Values outside 0..1 or not numbers are ignored; an explicit `-sps` in your arguments wins. | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_TEST_DUP_IDS` | Test switch. Makes picks 1 to N-1 of every token repeat pick 0, to check the plugin survives repeated expert ids. Changes the model's output, so never use it for real work. Used by `tests/dup_ids.sh`. | off (0; values of 1 or less do nothing) | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_TEST_POISON_READS` | Test switch. Each background expert read first fills its target with 0xFF bytes and waits (the `MOE_CACHE_TEST_READ_DELAY_US` time), to catch code that reads an expert before it has fully loaded. Any value except `0` turns it on. Slows loading. | off | internal/testing |
